Package: ldaR6
Type: Package
Title: Predictive Linear Discriminant Analysis with R6 and a Shiny Interface
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person(
    given = "Chancy Loïc Franlly",
    family = "MAMPOUYA CLARK",
    email = "clarkfranlly@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements predictive linear discriminant analysis (LDA) from
    scratch using an 'R6' class with methods for model fitting, class
    prediction, posterior probability estimation, and projection onto
    discriminant axes. The model uses a pooled within-class covariance
    matrix and configurable class priors. The package provides global and
    partial Wilks' lambda tests, Rao's F approximation, stepwise variable
    selection, categorical predictor encoding, optional covariance
    shrinkage, and cross-validation. A 'Shiny' application supports model
    training, result visualization, and individual or batch prediction.
